-- the spec's STLC
module STLC
  declared x
  declared Ty
  declared LC
  declared Ctx
warning: in the grammar of LC, production vacuous: x binds in nothing
-- a binding form's head is not a metavariable
refused: in the grammar of L, production bad: q is not a metavariable
-- a binder that is not a String
refused: in the grammar of L, production num: a binder must be a String, and n is an Int
-- an occurrence that is not a String
refused: in the grammar of L, production num: an occurrence must be a String, and n is an Int
-- a bracket naming what is not an argument
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: x is not an argument of f
-- a bracket naming an occurrence
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: x is an occurrence, so it binds nothing
-- a bracket naming what the declared binders do not
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: n is not one of the binders declared
-- metadata naming what is not written
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: x is not an argument of f
-- one argument written with two scopes
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: M is written with different binders free in it
-- a production with no items
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: it has no items
-- a metavariable named twice
refused: in the grammar of L: M is named twice
-- a metavariable that is already a token class
refused: in the grammar of L: x is already a metavariable or a token class
-- a language named like something declared
refused: x is already declared
-- a constructor named like something declared
refused: L's constructor x is already declared
-- two productions of one name
refused: L's constructor f is already declared
-- a context without one empty and one extension production
refused: in the context C: a context needs one production with no context slot and at least one with exactly one
-- a terminal that writes the placeholder
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: the terminal `█` contains the reserved █, which is how a part of a term that is not written yet is shown
-- a terminal that merely contains it
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: the terminal `a█b` contains the reserved █, which is how a part of a term that is not written yet is shown
-- a binder free in a language that reaches no such class
refused: in the grammar of L, production M.L.f: a binder is free in R, which is of M.P, and nothing M.P reaches occurs at M.x, so there is nothing there to rename
-- a token class that would read it
refused: in the grammar of L, production f: the token class any would read the reserved █, which is how a part of a term that is not written yet is shown
-- a block naming no installed grammar
refused: Nope is not a language, a context or a judgment that is declared
-- a block declaring a metavariable of its own
refused: in the notation for C: it may not declare the metavariable Z, because its productions are written in C's own
-- a production naming nothing declared
refused: in the notation for C, production nosuch: nosuch is not a declared function
-- a production naming another grammar's constructor
refused: in the notation for C, production Ty.base: Ty.base is already a production of a grammar
-- a production naming one the grammar already has
refused: in the notation for C, production ext: ext is already a production of a grammar
-- more slots than the function takes
refused: in the notation for C, production join: join takes 2 arguments and the notation has 3 slots
-- the same name for two of the arguments
refused: in the notation for C, production join: a names two of its arguments, and a name stands for one
-- a parameter the notation never writes
refused: in the notation for C, production join: b is not written in the notation, so that argument could not be given
-- a parameter naming an argument no notation reads
refused: in the notation for C, production lift: s names an argument of String, which no notation reads by itself — if it is a String, say which token class, as ( s : ‹class› )
-- a function that does not return the grammar's datatype
refused: in the notation for C, production dom: dom returns Joining.Ty.Ty, not a C
-- a production writing a binding form
refused: in the notation for C, production join: b is written as a binding form, and an application binds nothing
-- a production with metadata
refused: in the notation for C, production join: join is a function, so there is no constructor for the metadata to be about
-- a role in a block that only adds spellings
refused: in the notation for C, production ext: a role belongs to the block that installs the grammar, and Joining.C's is installed already, with its substitution generated from the roles it had then
-- a language named like the built-in tag surface
refused: surface is one of Thena's own tags, so a language may not take its name
-- a language named like the built-in tag core
refused: core is one of Thena's own tags, so a language may not take its name
-- no where
line 3: a block's first line names it and ends in where
-- metadata that is none of the three
line 4: x as whatever is not ‹x› as occurrence, ‹x› as binder or { ‹x›, … } as binders
-- a production with no arrow
line 4: a production is ‹name› -> ‹items›, or ‹name› : ‹metadata› -> ‹items›
-- a bracket never closed
line 4: a [ is never closed
-- a line indented less
line 5: this line is indented less than the productions above it
